# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Mirrors .gitignore. Real data must never be baked into an image layer, and
# must never reach the build context either: the daemon caches what it is sent,
# and a remote or rootless builder is off this machine entirely. The data
# directory is a bind mount at runtime, never a COPY.
#
# The `**/` prefixes are load-bearing and are why this file does not simply
# repeat .gitignore. The two formats look alike and match differently: a
# .gitignore pattern with no slash matches at every depth, while a .dockerignore
# pattern is matched against the whole path, so a bare `*.pdf` here covers
# `report.pdf` at the root and NOTHING below it. Every wildcard below is
# depth-qualified for that reason. Verified by building a probe context: with
# bare patterns, data.bak-*/incoming/report.pdf was sent to the daemon.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
data/
output/
# `make reset` renames ./data to data.bak-<timestamp> and leaves it in the
# checkout. It holds every report and the database — the exact contents of
# data/, under a name data/ does not match. .gitignore denies it; so must this.
data.bak-*/
**/*.sqlite
**/*.sqlite3
**/*.db
**/*.pdf
**/*.zip
**/*.csv
**/*.tsv
**/*.xls
**/*.xlsx
**/*.ods
**/*.doc
**/*.docx
**/*.eml
**/*.mbox
**/*.7z
**/*.rar
**/*.tar
**/*.tar.gz
**/*.tgz
tools/denylist.txt
**/*.local.*
.env

# gstack tool output: QA reports, design audits and screenshots. The screenshots
# are pictures of the app rendering real reports, which makes this directory as
# sensitive as data/ and, at 2 MB of PNGs, more likely to be noticed missing
# than noticed present.
.gstack/

# A container test bind-mounts this as /data. See .gitignore.
.pytest-layout-data/

.git/
.github/
__pycache__/
**/*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
**/*.egg-info/
dist/
build/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/

node_modules/
frontend/dist/
.vite/

.DS_Store
